shows in dermoscopy vascular lesions as well-defined red, purple, or blue areas with multiple round to oval lacunae, homogeneous hemorrhagic zones, and variable vessel morphologies such as dotted, linear-irregular or clustered glomerular vessels.
Dermoscopy shows vascular lesions as well-circumscribed red, purple, or blue structureless areas and lacunae, with variations including clustered dotted or linear vessels, serpentine or branching patterns, focal whitish septa, and mixed color intensity.
shows a dermoscopic view dominated by multiple round to oval red‑purple lacunae and homogeneous blotches, interspersed with dotted or linear serpentine vessels; color ranges from bright red to deep violet with occasional dark crusts.
Dermoscopic vascular lesions show clustered red to purple lacunae or structureless areas, from pinpoint dotted and linear serpentine vessels to larger globular or red-blue pools, often separated by pale whitish septa or pale background.
Dermoscopic vascular lesions appear as red to purple lacunae and homogeneous blotches; variation 5 shows multiple round to oval dark-red lacunae separated by pale septa, with occasional linear, dotted or arborizing vessels and varying hemorrhagic shades.
Numerous well‑circumscribed red to violaceous lacunae dominate the dermoscopic view, varying in size and depth, separated by pale septa, with occasional darker focal areas and scattered dotted or linear peripheral vessels.
In dermoscopy, vascular lesions appear as red-purple to blue structures ranging from pinpoint dotted and comma vessels to linear-irregular or clustered lacunae, often showing homogeneous or multi-lobulated areas with variable vessel density and occasional hemorrhagic spots.
Vascular lesions in dermoscopy appear as bright red to violaceous areas with round or oval lacunae, punctate dots, linear or serpentine vessels, and clustered globules, sometimes showing dusky blue shadows or diffuse homogeneous erythema.
Dermoscopy of vascular lesions reveals well‑circumscribed red to purple lacunae or globules, diffuse homogeneous red areas, and variable vessel morphologies (dotted, linear, arborizing, hairpin), with variations in size, color intensity, and clustering.
Dermoscopy reveals red to violaceous globules, lacunae and homogeneous areas, ranging from tiny dotted or pinpoint vessels to clustered round or oval lakes, with occasional linear, serpentine vessels and surface crusting.
